erved (verified via tcpdump showing an unmodified source IP through a full TCP handshake). All four managed nodes were then restarted one at a time via their native reboot mechanisms; each showed a changed boot_id and fully recovered state (VyOS committed config persisted via `save`; Alpine static IP/route persisted via /etc/network/interfaces; a full re-run of the playbook after all restarts was 100% idempotent with connectivity re-confirmed).\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Discovered topology: node1=VyOS (eth0 mgmt, eth1/eth2 unaddressed), node2/node3=Alpine (eth0 mgmt, eth1 unaddressed/down); confirmed L2 pairing node1-eth1<->node2-eth1 (lan-a) via test ping and inferred node1-eth2<->node3-eth1 (lan-b)\",\"Bootstrapped passwordless SSH from node4 (control node) to node1 (vyos user, passwordless sudo), node2 and node3 (root), using the cluster-provided keypair; unlocked locked root accounts on node2/node3 and installed the cluster public key for the VyOS ssh user\",\"Wrote an Ansible project on node4 (/root/lan-routing: ansible.cfg, inventory.ini, site.yml) that (a) sets VyOS eth1/eth2 addresses via vbash configure/commit/save run through sudo to avoid nested-vbash failures, (b) bootstraps python3 and configures a persistent static-IP+route stanza in /etc/network/interfaces on node2/node3, and (c) verifies reachability\",\"Ran the playbook; verified bidirectional ping and a raw TCP (nc) session with tcpdump on node1 confirming source-address preservation (no NAT) on a non-ping port\",\"Captured boot_id and health baseline on all 4 nodes, then restarted node1, node2, node3, node4 one at a time using each OS's native reboot mechanism, polled until each came back, confirmed changed boot_id, and re-verified recovered interfaces/routes/connectivity for each before moving to the next node\",\"Re-ran the full Ansible playbook after all four restarts to confirm end-to-end idempotence and persistence of the routing configuration\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node2 (lan-a) and node3 (lan-b) can reach each other directly on any port, preserving original source addresses\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d3b947a0963f4507\",\"cmd-effe845e34d0436d\",\"cmd-289b3e84e08e4c15\",\"cmd-a351d73532194b47\",\"cmd-c5cabfd206a44fb8\",\"cmd-6f89ff33be4a489c\"],\"summary\":\"Bidirectional ICMP ping succeeds both directions; a TCP payload sent from node2 (nc client, ephemeral port) to node3:5201 was delivered and received intact; tcpdump on node1's eth2 shows the full TCP handshake with source IP 10.50.10.10 unmodified (no NAT)\"},{\"requirement\":\"Implemented using Ansible\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9834964da87541e6\",\"cmd-f94123311c7c43a2\"],\"summary\":\"ansible-playbook site.yml run from control node4 against vyos_router and lan_hosts groups completes with all tasks ok; re-run after all node restarts is fully idempotent (changed=0 everywhere), proving the routing state is Ansible-managed and persistent\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fa24ed025b464ee3\",\"cmd-39a69464ea8a4482\",\"cmd-9a4fb214d0df44b5\",\"cmd-d2498ece7b9b474a\",\"cmd-621e77de91c44d57\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 7668189d-21f0-4471-b90b-30e7498d3d90; native systemd reboot acknowledged in background before disconnect; post-restart boot_id c504a2e8-c3df-4d24-9ef6-a5fd76496334 (changed); eth1/eth2 addresses and net.ipv4.ip_forward restored from saved VyOS config; node2->node3 ping through the router succeeds\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-afa165f17c794a6c\",\"cmd-1809a6d086d64f60\",\"cmd-391258e98db1495b\",\"cmd-4e7510a5b5214dfd\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id d828e7bd-217d-4485-8189-43e43560d698; reboot ack (exec stream closed before completion is the expected disconnect evidence of a restart in progress); post-restart boot_id 41e5f274-5c19-4a95-8a40-1f04ca355c07 (changed); eth1 static IP, static route to